11. Any of the following cardiovascular and cerebrovascular events within half a year before screening: unstable angina pectoris requiring hospitalization, myocardial infarction, coronary artery bypass grafting, percutaneous coronary intervention (diagnostic angiography is allowed), moderate to severe congestive heart failure (NYHA grade III or IV), atrial or ventricular arrhythmia requiring hospitalization (such as atrial fibrillation and ventricular tachycardia), pacemaker or defibrillator implantation, transient ischemic attack or cerebrovascular accident (e.g. stroke), or those with coronary artery bypass grafting or revascularization planned during the study period;
