reening, received a transfusion within 90 days prior to Screening, or plan to donate during the course of the study; 28. Positive for hepatitis B surface antigen, HIV antibody, or hepatitis C virus antibody at Screening; 29. Receipt of any investigational product within 30 days prior to first study drug administration (90 days for investigational biologic agents) or 5 half-lives, whichever is greater, or participation in \>3 clinical studies within 12 months; 30. Known or suspected hypersensitivity to PATAS or any components of the formulation used (sodium hydroxide or mannitol); or 31. Employee of the Sponsor, the CRO, or the clinical site (e.g., permanent employee, temporary contract worker, or designee responsible for the conduct of the study) or family members (e.g., spouse, parent, sibling, or child) of the Sponsor, CRO, or other clinical site employee

Inclusion Criteria:

